<title>INDIA: Indian cotton market closed for Hindu festival.</title>
<headline>Indian cotton market closed for Hindu festival.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's cotton market was closed on Friday for a Hindu religious holiday.</p>
<p>Prices are seen holding ground on expectations the government may allow fresh exports, dealers said.</p>
<p>On Thursday, Bengal-deshi rose 15 rupees to 840/890 per maund and Punjab saw-ginned 10 to 1,460/1,675.</p>
<p>Gujarat Kalyan (medium-staple) firmed 200 rupees to 11,500/11,700 per candy (355.56 kg).</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
